before:
```typescript
function addBonus(points: number): number {
  return points + 4;
}
console.log(addBonus(7));
```

This prints 11. addBonus receives 7, computes 7 + 4, and returns the number 11. It does not print by itself; the surrounding console.log displays its return value. The braces contain the body and return sends the result back to the caller.

after:
This function receives a number and gives back a number.
```typescript
function addBonus(points: number): number {
  return points + 4;
}
console.log(addBonus(7));
```
It receives 7, adds 4, and returns 11. Console.log shows that returned value.
